# {{ project_name }}

{{ description }}

A layered FastAPI service with health and readiness endpoints, JSON logs with request IDs, and
one error envelope
{%- if 'database' in components %}, SQLAlchemy persistence with Alembic migrations{% endif %}
{%- if 'worker' in components %}, background jobs{% endif %}
{%- if 'auth-api-key' in components %}, API-key authentication{% endif %}
{%- if 'auth-oidc' in components %}, OpenID Connect authentication{% endif %}.
It runs locally without any external service.

## Requirements

[uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) is the only tool you need. It installs Python {{ python_version }}+
and every development tool on demand, on Windows, macOS, and Linux.

## Getting started

```bash
uv sync                                  # create .venv with the dev group
uv lock                                  # create uv.lock, then commit it
{%- if 'database' in components %}
uv run alembic upgrade head              # create the local SQLite database
{%- endif %}
uv run {{ package_name }} serve --reload   # development server on http://127.0.0.1:8000
```

Open <http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs> for the interactive API documentation.
`/health/live` reports that the process is up, and `/health/ready` checks its dependencies.

## Configuration

Settings live in `{{ package_name }}/bootstrap/settings.py`. Override any of them with an
environment variable prefixed `{{ package_name|upper }}_`, or copy `.env.example` to `.env` for
local values. `.env` is git-ignored; never commit it.

In production, set `{{ package_name|upper }}_ENVIRONMENT=production` and the real
`{{ package_name|upper }}_ALLOWED_HOSTS`. Startup fails if a production setting is unsafe
{%- if 'database' in components %}, if `DATABASE_URL` is left at the local default{% endif %}
{%- if 'auth' in components %}, or if the authentication settings are missing{% endif %}.
{%- if 'database' in components %}

## Database

The default is a local SQLite file. For PostgreSQL, install the driver with
`uv sync --group postgres` and set
`{{ package_name|upper }}_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://user@host/db`.

| Task | Command |
| --- | --- |
| Apply migrations | `uv run alembic upgrade head` |
| Create a migration after changing `infrastructure/database/models.py` | `uv run alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe the change"` |
| Check that models and migrations agree | `uv run alembic check` |

Migrations never run on startup. Tests migrate a private SQLite file per test.
{%- endif %}
